Description: re-read the pull request before trusting a snapshot taken across the check queries
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

The facts are read once, then review threads and every check page are fetched
against them. A push, a base retarget, a new review or a draft toggle in that
window left the verdict standing on a SHA and a base the pull request no longer
had, so the watcher could report READY for a revision that had already been
superseded. The facts are read again after collection and the snapshot is
refused as retryable when anything the verdict depends on moved; GitHub
computing mergeability on demand is not such a change.

